      "message": "fix(circular): keep the helix entries of the rings apart\n\nA flat Circular runs every ring down the same level ladder. The helix\nof each ring therefore shares each level's depth band with the helix of\nevery other ring. With stepover 2 and helix radius 1, the helices\ntouched, and verification blocked the program with Crossing warnings.\n\nEach later ring now starts at a vertex of its own polygon where its\npredicted helix orbit keeps 0.01 mm from the orbits already flown.\nAfter each ring, the kernel reads the ring's descents with the crossing\nlaw itself. If one crosses an earlier ring's descent, the operation is\nrefused by name (\"helix entry: ...\"). Plunge, ramp and the vault mode do\nnot change.\n\nThe test module of circular.rs moves to circular_tests.rs (400-line\nlaw). Three circular_arcs rows that Crossing warnings held before now\nexpect the named refusal. The radius rows keep their gouge check on a\nplunge entry.\n\nFixes #3109\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
